On Sep 5, 2:23 pm, Andrew Fabbro <andrew.fab...@gmail.com> wrote:
> In the early game, I find a difficult balance between starving vs.
> fighting vs. healing.  It goes something like this:
>
> A. I need food, I'll go kill something and eat it.
>
> B. Whew, no longer hungry, but now I need to heal hit points.  I'll
> rest/try to avoid combat.
>
> C. Uh-oh, hungry again, better go do some more killing, even though my
> hit points haven't quite healed up...

A few things to try:

(a) kill things from a distance if you can -- no lowered HP, unless
they've got missile weapons too.
(b) Conserve food by praying when you get weak (or fainting) -- if
you're in good standing, your god will solve the problem. If I only
have a few items of food, I'll use this liberally until I get at least
four solid food items. Often I'll still do it for a while after by
alternating between solving hunger via prayer and solving it via
eating, one for one. This strategy doesn't always work well for
characters that may need prayer to solve other bigger problems,
though.




